OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group — placing files there would not compile.
The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`, where the
landed sibling P7 battery pages ship (EnergyPage, BatteryCellsPage, BatteryDegradationPage,
SleepEfficiencyPage — ledger status=done), and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source
path (createIntermediateGroups: true). Page hosting uses the proven `*RouteRegistration` pattern chained
in `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`. Tests live in `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Battery/`. Strings ship in
the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is
the only deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9 — identical to the
reconciliation used by every landed p4-apple P7 page.

The web route `/energy-flow` had NO `AppRoute` case; this prompt adds `.energyFlow` (pathSegment
`energy-flow`, group `.energy`, systemImage `powerplug.fill`) to `Sources/App/AppRoute.swift` so
`AppRouteParser` resolves `/energy-flow` + the deep link automatically, and wires the host in
`TeslaSyncApp.swift`. ("navigation registration" is an allowed file class.)

SYMBOL-COLLISION NOTE (covenant #1, real red caught + fixed): the first full xcodebuild surfaced 2
genuine redeclarations — my diagram sub-views `EnergyFlowNode` / `EnergyFlowArrow` collided with the
pre-existing widget structs of the same name in `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/EnergyFlowWidget.Models.swift`.
Renamed mine to `EnergyFlowDiagramNode` / `EnergyFlowDiagramArrow`; a full-codebase declaration scan
confirms every other EnergyFlow* symbol I introduce is unique (the widget namespace is crowded:
EnergyFlowModel/Node/Arrow/Diagram/ValueUnit/NodeID/... — all distinct from mine).

