================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI EnergyFlowPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
EnergyFlowPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/ready over an
injectable EnergyFlowDataSource seam (loadVehicles + loadStats(days) + loadFlow=useEnergyFlow), whose value
types mirror the web wire 1:1 (production binds the KMP core through the seam). The page reproduces the web
chrome (Energy-Flow title + subtitle + header VehicleSelect + presets RangePicker), the real-time energy-flow
schematic (the eight GlassPanels — outer frame, Grid source, Battery hub with its SoC TSRadialGauge, Motor
sink, and the DC/AC/HVAC/Accessories live-breakdown chips, plus the Charging/Driving flow arrows), polled in
real time (web refetchInterval: REALTIME) via a lifecycle .task loop with a >2-minute staleness indicator
(ADR-013); the six summary TSMetricCards; the daily-energy TSAreaChart; the paired daily-distance /
daily-efficiency TSBarCharts; the Efficiency-Metrics panel (avg-efficiency rating ladder + CO₂ + avg/day);
and the daily-energy-history TSDataTable — all from the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled
glass, no direct Charts/recharts, no WKWebView). Every data source implements loading/empty/error/success and
every section its own empty state; all 44 visible strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key
names. The web RadialGauge SoC maps to the shared TSRadialGauge (a 0–1 percentage gauge — exact fit). SI
watt-hours/metres convert to the user's units only at the render boundary via the shared Units facade
(ADR-005); the /energy/flow endpoint's wire-native kW/kWh are shown verbatim exactly as the web does.
Adaptive across macOS (regular) and iPhone (compact) via ViewThatFits + horizontalSizeClass.

Verified GREEN: swiftlint --strict (0), placeholder gate (0), isolated Foundation type-check (0), an executed
pure-logic harness (25/25), and the macOS app-target whole-module type-check (EmitSwiftModule, Swift 6
strict-concurrency complete, 0 diagnostics in any EnergyFlow file). The first full build caught 2 genuine
symbol redeclarations against the pre-existing EnergyFlow widget structs; both renamed and re-verified clean.
ZERO diagnostics in any EnergyFlow file.

